# CITATION.cff — Citation File Format 1.2.0
#
# v1.0.1. The Zenodo version DOI is minted when the GitHub release is published, so it is
# added in a follow-up commit (see the `identifiers:` block below); the concept DOI
# 10.5281/zenodo.23291758 always resolves to the newest version of this code archive.
#
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these result tables, please cite the manuscript and the archived release."
title: "A five-rung testability audit for public omics resources: code and key results"
type: software
version: "v1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yuanyuan20020329/sgrg-uc-testability-audit"

authors:
  - family-names: "Yuan"
    given-names: "Yike"
    email: "yyk20020329@126.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-8391-4134"
    affiliation: "Hubei University of Chinese Medicine, Wuhan, Hubei, China"
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Hongci"
    email: "chenhongci@hbhtcm.com"                      # corresponding author
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3335-8998"
    affiliation: "Hubei Provincial Hospital of Traditional Chinese Medicine, Wuhan, Hubei, China"

keywords:
  - testability
  - reproducibility
  - data provenance
  - batch confounding
  - pseudoreplication
  - single-cell genomics
  - Mendelian randomisation
  - ulcerative colitis
  - stress granules

abstract: >-
  Analysis code and key result tables for an ordered five-rung audit of whether
  public omics resources can support the claims made from them: rung 1 control
  provenance, rung 2 batch-disease nesting, rung 2' instrument independence,
  rung 3 technical-load confounding, rung 4 null-distribution calibration and
  rung 5 the power floor. The ladder is applied to a stress-granule-related gene
  set x ulcerative colitis claim and validated on two independent published
  claims (ferroptosis x hepatocellular carcinoma; pyroptosis x Parkinson's
  disease). No primary data are redistributed; accessions and retrieval scripts
  are provided.

identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23291758
    description: "Zenodo concept DOI of this code archive (resolves to the newest version)"

